  "title": "Signing a graph to have small magnitude eigenvalues",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If $A$ is the adjacency matrix of a $d$-regular graph, then there is a symmetric signing of $A$ (i.e. replace some $+1$ entries by $-1$ ) so that the resulting matrix has all eigenvalues of magnitude at most $2 \\sqrt{d-1}$.",
